{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "pw8-wt-morph",
    "name": "WT MORPH",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "The first preset to actually exercise the Wavetable engine end to end: OP0 reads content/wavetables/basic_harmonic.json (a real, FFT-mip-mapped table generated by pw8-wavetable-builder from a synthesized sine-to-40th-harmonic-sawtooth source, see scripts/generate_test_wavetable_source.py). A slow LFO continuously sweeps the wavetable frame position (Lfo1 -> OperatorWavetablePosition), the signature 'evolving wavetable' motion. Mip selection happens per-sample based on the actual note frequency and render sample rate, so this preset also demonstrates the anti-aliasing this pass added.",
    "category": "lead",
    "moods": [
      "digital",
      "evolving",
      "bright"
    ],
